    "final_verdict": "VERDICT: CHANGES REQUESTED\n\nThe field rename, the `luhn` extraction into a shared private primitive, `locality` delegating to the new `regionOf`, and the audit/event/schema/OpenAPI updates are all coherent and idiomatic. One structural issue remains:\n\n**Duplicated memberId-parsing loop across `regionOf` and `fiscalYear(String)`** (`Owner.java:683-692` and `Owner.java:831-844`). Both methods independently re-implement the identical \"skip the leading run of letters\" scan to locate the end of the REGION segment:\n\n```java\nint i = 0;\nwhile (i < memberId.length() && Character.isLetter(memberId.charAt(i))) {\n    i++;\n}\n```\n\nEach now encodes its own copy of the knowledge that \"REGION is the leading letters, and the FY segment starts right after them.\" That is the same `memberId` layout parsed in two places; if the format ever shifts, both loops must change in lockstep. This is exactly the kind of duplication the unification was meant to avoid \u2014 note `locality` was correctly collapsed to delegate to `regionOf`, but `fiscalYear(String)` was not given the same treatment.\n\nSuggested fix: extract a single private helper that returns the region-segment boundary (the index after the leading letters), e.g.:\n\n```java\nprivate static int regionEnd(String memberId) {\n    int i = 0;\n    while (i < memberId.length() && Character.isLetter(memberId.charAt(i))) {\n        i++;\n    }\n    return i;\n}\n```\n\nThen have `regionOf` build its result from `regionEnd(...)` (`i == 0 ? \"UNKNOWN\" : memberId.substring(0, i)`) and have `fiscalYear(String)` read `start = regionEnd(memberId)` instead of its own loop. That keeps the memberId's segment layout defined in exactly one place, matching how `locality`/`regionOf` already share.",
